$text="# Rent Guardian implementation report — 9 October 2026 (Asia/Dhaka)\n\n";
$text.="This report distinguishes new changes from the existing app. The entire V1.0 source story extraction (161 stories) was read and compared with its source DOCX. The React/Vite, PHP/PDO and MariaDB architecture was retained. No production deployment or live payment was made. Acceptance of the complete master prompt remains PARTIALLY COMPLETED.\n\n";
$text.="## A. Actual changes\n\n- All portals: shared 18 px desktop and 17 px mobile body text, 16 px secondary text, 30–32 px page headings, visible focus rings and practical 44 px controls. Cards, forms, tables, review screens and navigation reflow on narrow screens.\n- Owner/tenant listing capability: private database drafts, recovery after reload, a review step, listing preview, no invented bedroom or size defaults, retained included utilities during editing, and readable View details actions. Publication is rejected while a tenancy/application remains open.\n- Property photography: no unrelated fallback for absent photos; explicit demo labels; multi-file selection, previews, browser WebP conversion capped at 2400 px, categories/captions, cover selection, ordered navigation, thumbnails, touch swipe, fullscreen controls and archived removal. Server checks image MIME, actual dimensions, 10 MB and 40 megapixel limits, 30 active photos and ownership. Removed uploads cannot be fetched from their file routes.\n- Tenant privacy: public results conceal exact house/road/floor/flat and coordinates; confirmed viewing participants, owners, assigned agents and authorized tenancy participants retain appropriate access. Uploads must reference the same property as their tenancy.\n- Renting: fixed the reserved-property verification upload permission; advance invoices are separate and due on move-in; unrelated paid invoices cannot satisfy the advance; repeated activation is rejected; approved police documents must belong to the designated head tenant. Move-out cannot close before its recorded date.\n- Finance/services: BDT fractional amounts remain visible, paid orders require a reviewed refund/adjustment before cancellation, and catering enrollment requires an active tenancy and verified active provider.\n- Search: independent server filters for division/district/area/sub-area, paginated results in groups of 24, and protection against stale search responses.\n\n";
$text.="## B. UI verification\n\nThe browser suite checks guest discovery, filtering, property reports, conceptual-model controls, tenant routes, owner listing access, provider tabs, supervisor, finance, field agent, and every administrator tab. The priority suite additionally exercises draft persistence, listing review/submission, the absent-photo state, optimized upload/removal and readable text at 375, 390, 768, 1024 and 1440 pixels. The mobile portal suite checks 26 routes across eight roles at 390 pixels. Tablet caption and signed-in header overflow were found and repaired. See verification.md for final command outcomes.\n\n";
$text.="## C. Database changes\n\n`server/migrate.php` safely adds `property_photos.category`, nullable `deleted_at`, and `photo_order(property_id,deleted_at,sort_order,id)`. It creates `listing_drafts`, keyed by user with a foreign key, JSON text payload and update timestamp. The user_stories implementation_status field now supports the five requested audit statuses, preserving source story text and conservatively replacing older heuristic labels. The schema for fresh setup contains the same structures. Existing properties, photo bytes, documents and historical financial records are preserved. Upload and photo ordering changes use transactions and parent-row locks. New advance invoices reuse the existing unique invoice billing-group model. No resets or destructive production migrations were performed.\n\n";
$text.="## D. Property listing audit\n\n| Measure | Count |\n|---|---:|\n| Persistent property records, including marked QA fixtures | {$counts['total']} |\n| Persistent records excluding QA_TEST fixtures | {$counts['non_qa']} |\n| Published records, including QA fixtures | {$counts['published']} |\n| Published records excluding QA fixtures | {$counts['published_non_qa']} |\n| Marked QA property fixtures | {$counts['qa']} |\n| Non-QA properties with active owner-upload file routes and no demo caption | $uploads |\n| Properties with supplied and independently verified authentic photographs | 0 |\n| Non-QA properties without verified authentic photographs | {$counts['non_qa']} |\n\nThe supplied database is a local demo. An uploaded file route is not proof that a photograph depicts the property. Existing sample photographs and generated QA files do not count as authentic. Demo seeders are restricted to the local environment; there is no separate deployed production dataset. A production export must exclude all demo/QA accounts and records and obtain genuine property-specific assets.\n\n";
$text.="## E. Full user-story traceability\n\nStatuses below are conservative: PARTIALLY COMPLETED means a local implementation exists but not every story outcome and exception is independently proven. BLOCKED identifies an unavailable external service or genuine tour asset. A module test reference is evidence for its tested portion, not a claim that every story in the module passed. No story is marked complete solely because a page or table exists.\n\n| # | Persona | Exact source requirement | Status | Implementation | Evidence / limitation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n";
$coverage="# User story coverage — audited 9 October 2026\n\nThis register supersedes the earlier heuristic implemented labels. See implementation-report.md for the full audit and test scope. Every source row is listed; module evidence does not mean every outcome of that story has been verified.\n\n| # | Persona | Requirement | Status | Implementation | Evidence / limitation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n";
foreach($stories as $s){
 $status='PARTIALLY COMPLETED';$entry=$map[$s['module']]??['src/pages/Workspace.jsx, server/api.php','No dedicated complete story test'];
 if($s['module']==='virtual_tour'){$status='BLOCKED';$entry[1]='No authentic scanned property tour supplied; conceptual scene clearly labelled.';}
 elseif(preg_match('/through call|through phone|push notification|guys to contact me/i',$s['want_to'])){$status='BLOCKED';$entry[1]='Callback requests persist; operational phone/push delivery is not configured.';}
 elseif(preg_match('/instant support.*1 hour/i',$s['want_to'])){$status='BLOCKED';$entry[1]='Matching exists; no real dispatch capacity or guaranteed one-hour arrival.';}
 run('UPDATE user_stories SET implementation_status=? WHERE id=?',[$status,$s['id']]);
 $escape=fn($v)=>str_replace(["|","\n","\r"],['/', ' ',' '],(string)$v);
 $line='| '.$s['id'].' | '.$escape($s['persona']).' | '.$escape($s['want_to']).' | '.$status.' | '.$escape($entry[0]).' | '.$escape($entry[1])." |\n";$text.=$line;$coverage.=$line;
